<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">10 events that happened on 1 May, from 305 to 2011.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">International Workers' Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Observed in over 160 countries, International Workers' Day commemorates the 1886 Haymarket affair in Chicago and celebrates the global labour movement's historic struggles for fair wages, safe conditions, and workers' rights.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">305 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,721 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Diocletian and Maximian abdicate together</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In ceremonies at Nicomedia and Milan, the two senior emperors stepped down in favour of Galerius and Constantius. The planned handover soon broke down into civil war among their successors.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diocletian">Diocletian</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1328 CE <span class="tih-ago">698 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">England ratifies the Treaty of Edinburgh-Northampton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting at Northampton, the English Parliament ratified the treaty recognising Robert the Bruce as king of an independent Scotland. It ended the First War of Scottish Independence, though peace did not last.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1707 CE <span class="tih-ago">319 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Acts of Union create the Kingdom of Great Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The union of England and Scotland took effect, creating a single kingdom and a single Parliament at Westminster. Scotland kept its own legal system and established church.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Kingdom of Great Britain</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1776 CE <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Adam Weishaupt founds the Bavarian Illuminati</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Law professor Adam Weishaupt founded a secret society to spread Enlightenment ideas in Catholic Bavaria. It was banned in the 1780s but has lived on in conspiracy theories ever since.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1840 CE <span class="tih-ago">186 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain issues the Penny Black, the first adhesive stamp</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Penny Black went on sale, valid for postage from 6 May. Prepaid at a flat rate under Rowland Hill's reforms, it made letters affordable for ordinary people.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1886 CE <span class="tih-ago">140 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">American workers strike for an eight-hour day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hundreds of thousands of workers across the United States walked out to demand an eight-hour day. Events in Chicago that week, culminating at Haymarket, led to 1 May becoming International Workers' Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1931 CE <span class="tih-ago">95 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Empire State Building opens in New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Hoover pressed a button in Washington to switch on the lights of the newly finished skyscraper. At 381 metres it remained the world's tallest building for nearly forty years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1960 CE <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet missile downs a US U-2 spy plane</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A U-2 piloted by Francis Gary Powers was shot down near Sverdlovsk. Washington's initial cover story collapsed when Moscow produced the pilot, wrecking the Paris summit two weeks later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2003 CE <span class="tih-ago">23 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George W. Bush declares major combat in Iraq over</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking aboard USS Abraham Lincoln beneath a 'Mission Accomplished' banner, the president announced the end of major combat operations. The insurgency that followed made the moment notorious.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2011 CE <span class="tih-ago">15 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US special forces kill Osama bin Laden in Pakistan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Navy SEALs raided a compound in Abbottabad and killed the al-Qaeda leader behind the 11 September attacks. President Obama announced it that night, US time; in Pakistan it was early on 2 May.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
